    "rationale": "This is the negative of the definite integral."
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "content": "$F(b) + F(a)$",
    "rationale": "The value at the lower limit is subtracted, not added."
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "content": "$F(b) - F(a) + c$",
    "rationale": "The constant cancels in the subtraction, so a definite integral has no + c."
   }
  ],
  "explanation": "$\\int_{a}^{b} f(x)\\,dx = \\Big[F(x)\\Big]_{a}^{b} = F(b) - F(a)$.",
